{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And you shall overlay it with pure gold.</b> From here is a hint to the three blessings of Grace after Meals from the Torah: זה\"ב — 'ז' ברכת הזן את העולם' (7 = the blessing 'Who nourishes the world'), 'ה' הארץ' (5 = for the land), 'ב' בונה ירושלים' (2 = Who builds Jerusalem)." "<b>And you shall make for it a crown of gold.</b> In the words זר זהב you will find a hint to the kingdom of the house of David." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: the Table with a crown of gold is a hint to the attribute of Judgment above, and therefore it was placed in the north, which is the left, and it is written (Job 37:22) מצפון זהב יאתה. And this is the meaning of 'whoever wishes to grow rich should face north' — he should intend toward the attribute of the north, which is Gevurah. And therefore there were upon the Table two coverings: one of scarlet wool (שני) and one of blue (תכלת) — the שני corresponding to the attribute of Judgment above; the תכלת corresponding to the attribute of Judgment below, which is included within all the attributes. And so the matter was: first they would place the showbread directly upon the Table itself with no intermediary, as it is written (Numbers 4:7–8) ולחם התמיד עליו יהיה — and it lay entirely upon the Table itself; and they would spread over the bread a covering of תכלת, and over this covering they would place all the utensils of the Table, and afterward they would spread over the utensils and the Table a covering of תולעת, and above it all was a covering of שני on top and a covering of תכלת below — corresponding to the attribute of Judgment above and the attribute of Judgment below. If so, these two attributes are hinted at in the Table through the two coverings, for the attribute of Judgment above bestows power upon that of below, which is called Malkhut and is hinted at in the word זהב, in which there is a hint to David, encompassing the kingdom of the house of David below; also the kingdom above — דוד מלך ישראל חי וקיים. And it is known that blessing of provision and abundance depends upon Malkhut, in the manner of what is written (Esther 1:7) ויין מלכות רב כיד המלך, and likewise the Sages, of blessed memory, said: the Table is a sign for the crown of the kingdom above. And the upshot of the matter is that from there comes the sustenance to nourish the world, ובשפלים, for it is the attribute that gives טרף לביתה וחק לנערותיה." "<b>And from here</b> you will understand the reason that the height of the Table together with its frame was 10 handbreadths. And behold, the Table with all that is upon it alludes to both of them (the attributes of Judgment above and below). And understand this."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:04:27.038915753Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}